    "questionText": "A bag contains 6 black chips and 4 red chips. Three chips are drawn at random without replacement. What is the probability that exactly two of the drawn chips are black?",
    "options": {
      "A": "3/10",
      "B": "2/5",
      "C": "3/5",
      "D": "1/2 (50%)"
    },
    "correctAnswer": "D",
    "correctAnswerText": "1/2 (50%)",
    "explanation": "Total chips = 10. Sample space = C(10, 3) = (10 * 9 * 8) / (3 * 2 * 1) = 120.\nFavorable outcomes = C(6, 2) * C(4, 1) = 15 * 4 = 60.\nProbability = 60 / 120 = 1/2 = 50%.",
